  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building Social Protection 2019-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kapacitetsbyggande sociala trygghetssystem 2019-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen g&#xe4;ller st&#xf6;d om 122 000 000 SEK till den andra fasen av Joint UN Programme on Social Protection under &#xe5;ren 2019 - 2024. Avtalspart &#xe4;r UNICEF och medverkande FN-organisationer &#xe4;r WFP, ILO och UNDP. Den f&#xf6;rsta fasen genomf&#xf6;rdes mellan 2016 och 2019 och fick st&#xf6;d av Finland, Irland, UK samt Sverige. Forts&#xe4;ttningen bygger vidare p&#xe5; resultat och erfarenheter fr&#xe5;n den f&#xf6;rsta fasen och har ett n&#xe5;got sn&#xe4;vare fokus p&#xe5; i f&#xf6;rsta hand att bygga system och kapacitet kring socialbidragssystemet f&#xf6;r de allra fattigaste i Zambia. Ytterligare viktiga komponenter &#xe4;r integrering av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, anpassning f&#xf6;r funktionshindrade, f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad nutrition f&#xf6;r gravida och ammande kvinnor samt system f&#xf6;r &#xf6;kade utvecklingseffekter genom f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade l&#xe4;nkar mellan socialbidrag och andra insatser sk Cash+. En ytterligare komponent g&#xe4;ller utbetalning av extra socialbidrag under 2019, 2020 och 2021 till mottagare i distrikt som &#xe4;r s&#xe4;rskilt drabbade av torka och Covid 19. Programmets ska finansieras gemensamt av Sverige, UK och Schweiz.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the second phase of the Joint UN Programme on Social Protection 2019-2024. Agreement partner is UNICEF and the participating UN Organisations are WFP and ILO. The first phase was implemented between 2016 and 2019 and was supported by Finland, Ireland, UK and Sweden. The continuation builds upon the results and lessons learned in the first phase but is more focused on building systems and capacity around the social cash transfers for the poorest in Zambia. Other important Components of the programme are mainstreaming of gender and disability, improved nutrition for pregnant and lactating mothers as well as increased development effects through enhanced operational links between social cash transfers and other initiatives, so called cash+. An additional component deals with Emergecy Cash Transfers during 2019, 2020 and 2021 to households that are hardest hit by the prolonged reduced rainfalls as well as Covid 19. The programme is to be funded by Sweden, UK and Switzerland.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint UN Programme on Social Protection phase II has the following expected results:

Impact:
Reduced Multi-dimentional poverty

Outcomes:&#xa0;
1. Predictable and regular Social Cash Transfers
2. Operational Cash linkages
3. Improved nutrition
4. Disability mainstreaming
5. Improved cluster perfomace
In addition the programme has a component of Emergency Cash Transfers with payments during 2019 and 2020 to social cash beneficiaries in the districts hardest hit by the prolonged reduced rainfall.In 2020 another round of Emergency Cash Transfers has been added to mitigate the situation related to Covid-19. Sida plan to contribute financially to the covid-19 ECT through an amendment to the programme agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
